Rules:
  [T1] Integration tests MUST use real dependencies (test databases).
  [T2] Use Testcontainers for ephemeral test environments.
  [T3] Clean up resources after each test.
  [T4] Tests MUST be idempotent — can run in any order.
  [T5] Use Docker Compose for multi-service test setups.
  [T6] Mock only external third-party APIs, not internal services.
  [T7] Set reasonable timeouts for integration tests.
  [T8] Run integration tests in CI/CD pipeline.

Pros:
  - Higher confidence
  - Catches integration issues
  - Tests real scenarios

Cons:
  - Slower execution
  - More complex setup
  - Maintenance overhead

Alternatives:
  - Contract testing
  - Component testing

State: +

